The initialization guard `if (!g.BackgroundTheme.getCurrent)` was always false because `getCurrent` exists immediately when the module loads (defined in IIFE), before `init()` is ever called. This prevented initialization, leaving `currentTheme` null and causing preload fallback to `daily-background.png` at all times.

## Changes

**`src/startup/flow.js` (lines 89-134)**
- Remove faulty existence check; call `init({ bus })` unconditionally (idempotent)
- Force immediate theme update with `updateTheme(true)` after init
- Handle async Promise return with `.then()` chaining
- Add telemetry event `startup_bgtheme_first_update`
- Wrap in try/catch to prevent startup disruption

**Before:**
```javascript
if (!g.BackgroundTheme.getCurrent) {  // Always false - getCurrent exists from IIFE
  g.BackgroundTheme.init({ bus });     // Never executes
}
// Result: currentTheme = null, preload falls back to daily-background.png
```

**After:**
```javascript
g.BackgroundTheme.init({ bus });
const firstTheme = g.BackgroundTheme.updateTheme(true);
firstTheme.then(t => {
  console.info('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update complete:', t);
  g.Telemetry.log('startup_bgtheme_first_update', { theme: t.key, reason: t.reason });
});
// Result: currentTheme populated, preload uses correct night-background.png at 23:00
```

**Test coverage:**
- `test_bgtheme_init_fix.html` - Integration tests verifying theme population after init
- `manual_verification.html` - Interactive verification page for visual testing

