## Problem
After merging PR #590 (adaptive background theming + namespace fix), the night background still does not appear at 23:00 local time (Sofia). Manual observation shows the Intro Hub still preloads `daily-background.png`. Root cause: In `src/startup/flow.js`, the initialization block for `BackgroundTheme` incorrectly treats the presence of the `getCurrent` method as proof the module was already initialized:
```javascript
// Current code (lines 89–98)
if (g.BackgroundTheme && typeof g.BackgroundTheme.init === 'function') {
  if (!g.BackgroundTheme.getCurrent) {
    g.BackgroundTheme.init({ bus });
    console.info('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme initialized');
  } else {
    console.info('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme already initialized, skipping');
  }
  // Sync adaptive setting ...
}
```
However, `backgroundTheme.js` defines `getCurrent` before `init()` is ever called (the IIFE sets up public functions up front). Therefore the guard always concludes the service is "already initialized" and skips `init()`. No initial `updateTheme()` runs, leaving `currentTheme` as `null`, causing the preload fallback to `daily-background.png`.

## Required Changes
1. Unconditionally call `g.BackgroundTheme.init({ bus })` during core service initialization.
2. Immediately force a first theme calculation with `g.BackgroundTheme.updateTheme(true)` so that `currentTheme` is populated before preloading the Intro Hub background.
3. Retain adaptive setting synchronization afterward.
4. Add defensive try/catch around these calls to avoid startup disruption if the module throws.
5. Emit a distinct log line (and optional telemetry event `startup_bgtheme_first_update`) confirming the first theme key and reason.
6. (Optional) If `currentTheme` is still null after forced update, log a warning. This helps future debugging.

## Acceptance Criteria
- After hard refresh at a night hour (e.g., 23:00 local timezone), `window.game.BackgroundTheme.getCurrent().key === 'night'` (or an override such as `rain`/`snow`/holiday depending on conditions).
- Console sequence shows:
  - `[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme init called (idempotent)`
  - `[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update complete: {key: "night", reason: "time-of-day (night)" ...}`
- Intro Hub preload log uses the night background URL (e.g., `assets/skins/night-background.png`).
- Manual override (`manualOverride('sunset')`) still works post-init.
- No regression to other startup behavior; tests pass.

## Proposed Code Change
Modify the BackgroundTheme init block in `src/startup/flow.js` to remove the incorrect guard and force first update. Replace existing lines 89–104 with:
```javascript
// Initialize BackgroundTheme service unconditionally (idempotent)
if (g.BackgroundTheme && typeof g.BackgroundTheme.init === 'function') {
  try {
    g.BackgroundTheme.init({ bus });
    console.info('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme init called (idempotent)');
  } catch (e) {
    console.warn('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme init failed', e);
  }

  // Sync adaptive setting (if present in config)
  const adaptiveSetting = g.game?.cfg?.adaptiveBackground;
  if (adaptiveSetting !== undefined) {
    try {
      g.BackgroundTheme.setAdaptive(adaptiveSetting);
    } catch (e) {
      console.warn('[StartupFlow] setAdaptive failed', e);
    }
  }

  // Force first theme update to ensure currentTheme is ready before any preload
  try {
    const firstTheme = g.BackgroundTheme.updateTheme(true);
    // If updateTheme returns a promise (async), handle it
    if (firstTheme && typeof firstTheme.then === 'function') {
      firstTheme.then(t => {
        if (t) {
          console.info('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update complete:', t);
          if (g.Telemetry && typeof g.Telemetry.log === 'function') {
            g.Telemetry.log('startup_bgtheme_first_update', { theme: t.key, reason: t.reason });
          }
        } else {
          console.warn('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update returned null');
        }
      }).catch(err => console.warn('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update promise failed', err));
    } else if (firstTheme) {
      console.info('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update complete:', firstTheme);
      if (g.Telemetry && typeof g.Telemetry.log === 'function') {
        g.Telemetry.log('startup_bgtheme_first_update', { theme: firstTheme.key, reason: firstTheme.reason });
      }
    } else {
      console.warn('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update returned null');
    }
  } catch (e) {
    console.warn('[StartupFlow] BackgroundTheme first update failed', e);
  }
}
```

## Additional Validation / Test Updates
- Add a small integration test (if test harness exists) to assert that after requiring `startup/flow.js` and calling `StartupFlow.init()`, `BackgroundTheme.getCurrent()` is non-null.
- Optionally update `test_intro_screen.html` to log initial theme key & reason right after initialization.

